From 5da1172545696ece1d9ffd2d6e100259e924dd0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guillaume Dumoulin <dev@myrole.fr>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:10:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] qtfb: collapsible widget cards; a finer window bar, card and
 pill

A tap on a widget card's header (a press and release that moves less
than the 12 px drag threshold; a drag still moves the card) collapses
the card to its header: the client is told it is hidden (visibility 0)
and sends nothing; another tap expands it and sends visibility 2 again.
The collapsed state is saved per app id with the position in
widget-positions.json ("collapsed": true) and restored the next time
the app shows its widget. No new message.

The window bar, the widget card and the minimized pill share one look:
64 px cells (touch targets), 30 px icons with Lucide's stroke width 2,
a 2 px outline, a 1.5 px hairline under the header, a 12 px radius for
the card and the pill, the name at 15 pt, and no boxed buttons. The
card's content sits 6 px inside the outline, clear of the corners.
